meta {
  name: Create Formula Attribute - Account Limit Reached (422)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "wc_test_formula",
    "type": "FormulaAttribute",
    "formula_str": "IF(price>0,\"has price\",\"no price\")"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 422
  res.body.errors[0].description: contains formula attributes
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account". **Real
  status-gating rule found** (first one for this project -- previously
  `config/api-testing.config.md`'s "Status-gating rules" table was empty):

  `{"data":[],"errors":[{"name":"ValidationError","description":"This
  account reached the limit of 2 formula attributes"}]}` -- this Dev
  account already has 2 pre-existing `FormulaAttribute`s (read-only
  fixtures), and this is a genuine plan/account-level cap, not a bug. The
  request body itself is otherwise valid (matches
  `FormulaAttributeCreateInputDto`, and `formula_str` syntax follows
  `materials/help-center/operations/if.md`'s `IF()` operator) -- this was
  never tested against a fresh/unlimited account, so the create path
  itself for `FormulaAttribute` remains **unconfirmed as working**; only
  the limit-enforcement 422 is confirmed. Worth flagging to Plytix/the
  user: is there a way to raise this limit on the Dev account so
  `FormulaAttribute` creation can actually be exercised?
}
